<%# The server rail. Sits beside the navigation rail, inside the same frame: the
    band's bottom hairline runs across the top of it and the navigation rail's own
    divider is its right edge, so the two read as one object split by a line rather
    than as two bars standing next to each other. Because this document is RTL,
    "beside" means to the left -- there is no room to the right of a rail that is
    already on the window's right edge.

    A server you can manage but the bot is not in is drawn and not linked. That is
    the whole point of the rail: it should tell you the server is yours and what is
    missing, and there is nothing to open yet. So it is an <a> with no href plus
    role="link" aria-disabled -- a link-shaped thing that says no. A real href would
    land on a page with nothing in it; a <span> would read as broken text. No href
    also keeps it out of the tab order by itself, and the tooltip still works,
    which matters because the tooltip is what explains the refusal.

    No `title` attribute on purpose. The label is drawn by one element on <body>
    that js/shell.js moves into place -- see .rail-tip -- and style.css puts a
    second tooltip on everything titled, so the two would stack. aria-label
    carries the accessible name, data-tip the one string that is not always the
    same thing as the name.

    Row order is the session's, not alphabetical: /guilds and /home present the
    same list in the same order, and a rail that reorders on its own puts the same
    server in three different places.

    The first row is not a server. It is the way back out, drawn above them and
    always present, because the rail is the only column that survives entering a
    server: everything in the menu is that server, so a server with no exit in it
    is a dead end you have to guess your way out of. Being first rather than last
    is what says which of the two groups it belongs to, and a hairline under it
    says the rest of the way.

    It carries the is-current state on /home for the same reason every row in this
    rail does: one column, one question -- where am I -- and an entry that is on
    the page you are already reading should say so rather than sit there looking
    unpressed. -%>
<%# var, not const: an include() is compiled into the including template's body,
    and about.ejs and home.ejs both have their own locals. -%>
<% currentPage = typeof currentPage !== 'undefined' ? currentPage : '' %>
<% var railRows = typeof railGuilds !== 'undefined' && railGuilds ? railGuilds : [] %>
<% if (railRows.length) { %>
<nav class="guild-rail" id="guildRail" aria-label="الرئيسية والسيرفرات">
  <div class="guild-rail-scroll">
    <%# .guild-rail-item so the tile, the "you are here" bar, the press and the
        tooltip are the ones every other row in this rail already has, rather than
        a second set of them here that can drift. First child, so it is also the
        first row of the arrival ladder -- which is the order it reads in. -%>
    <a class="guild-rail-item guild-rail-home<%= currentPage === 'home' ? ' is-current' : '' %>"
       href="/home"
       aria-label="الرئيسية"<% if (currentPage === 'home') { %> aria-current="page"<% } %>
       data-tip="الرئيسية">
      <span class="guild-rail-ava">
        <i class="fas fa-house" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </span>
    </a>
    <% railRows.forEach(function (g) { %>
    <% var current = !!(locals.guild && String(locals.guild.id) === g.id); %>
    <a class="guild-rail-item<%= current ? ' is-current' : '' %><%= g.inBot ? '' : ' is-off' %>"
       <% if (g.inBot) { %>href="/guilds/<%= g.id %>"<% } else { %>role="link" aria-disabled="true"<% } %>
       aria-label="<%= g.name %>"
       data-tip="<%= g.inBot ? g.name : g.name + ' — البوت مو موجود بهالسيرفر' %>">
      <span class="guild-rail-ava<%= g.icon ? '' : ' noimg' %>">
        <% if (g.icon) { %>
        <%# The parent is read BEFORE the node is detached -- remove() nulls parentNode,
            so the class was never added and the letter underneath never appeared. -%>
        <img src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/icons/<%= g.id %>/<%= g.icon %>.png?size=128" alt="" loading="lazy"
             onerror="var p=this.parentNode;this.remove();p.classList.add('noimg')">
        <% } %>
        <span class="guild-rail-letter"><%= g.name.charAt(0) %></span>
      </span>
    </a>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
</nav>
<% } %>
